You maintain a SQL knowledge base for a data agent. Given a user question and the SQL that answered it, draft a YAML document in strict YAML (no markdown fences, no commentary) with this shape:

example:
  question: <the question>
  sql: <the complete SQL on ONE single line>
  tags: [<2-4 short topic tags>]
terms:
  - term: <a business term appearing in the question>
    mapping: <table-qualified SQL expression, every column prefixed with its table, e.g. AVG(students.grade) or COUNT(students.id)>
    tables: [<tables involved>]
    definition: <one-line definition>

IMPORTANT: every value must be on a single line with correct YAML indentation. Never continue a value on an unindented line. Every column reference in `mapping` MUST be qualified with its table name — the table binding is derived from the expression.